  kids: {
    tasbihp: 'Now you praise Allah lots of times in a row: “Subḥāna llāh, al-ḥamdu li-llāh, lā ilāha illa llāh, Allāhu akbar.” Count quietly on your fingers – like a little song for saying thank you.',
    sahw: 'Everyone forgets something sometimes – even in prayer. That’s okay! If, for example, you forgot to sit after the second rakʿah, you simply do two extra prostrations at the end. Then everything is fine again.',
    ghuslParts: {
      heart: 'Ghusl is a big washing for the whole body. Grown-ups do it in certain situations, and many also on Friday or before Eid. Say in your heart: “I am now washing my whole body for Allah” – and then “Bismillāh”.',
      hands: 'First you wash your hands – three times, between the fingers too.',
      private: 'Then, with your left hand, you wash the parts your underwear covers until they are clean. After that you wash your hands again.',
      wuduAll: 'Now you do the normal ablution you already know: hands, mouth, nose, face, arms, head, ears and feet.',
      mouth: 'Rinse your mouth really well so the water reaches everywhere – three times.',
      nose: 'And your nose too: gently draw in water and blow it out, three times.',
      headPour: 'Now pour water over your head, three times. The water should reach the skin under your hair – rub long hair well.',
      sideR: 'Then the right side of your body: from the shoulder all the way down to the foot, three times. Right always comes first.',
      sideL: 'Now the left side the same way, three times.',
      body: 'Finally, check that really no spot stays dry: belly button, behind the ears, under the arms, between fingers and toes. Like in the shower – only very mindfully.',
    },
    tayammumParts: {
      heart: 'Sometimes there is no water – for example on a hike – or someone is ill and must not get wet. Then tayammum helps: you get ready with clean earth. Say in your heart: “I am doing tayammum for the prayer” – and “Bismillāh”.',
      strike: 'Place both hands flat on clean earth, sand or a stone.',
      dust: 'Tap your hands lightly or blow – you shouldn’t get dirty, the earth should only touch your hands.',
      tFace: 'Wipe both hands once over your whole face, from the forehead to the chin.',
      strike2: 'Place your hands on the earth once more and tap them off.',
      tArmR: 'Wipe your left hand over your right arm, from the fingers to the elbow.',
      tArmL: 'And your right hand over your left arm, up to the elbow. Done – now you may pray!',
    },
    niyya: 'Stand calmly and look at the spot where your forehead will soon touch the floor. Say in your heart: “I am now praying for Allah.” This is the niyya, the intention – you don’t have to say it out loud.',
    takbir: 'Raise both hands until your thumbs almost touch your ears and say: “Allāhu akbar” – Allah is greater than everything. Now you are in the prayer: you don’t talk to others and you don’t look around.',
    opening: 'Place your right hand over your left and stand still like a tree. Now you praise Allah very quietly – just like greeting someone kindly before you ask them for something.',
    fatiha: 'Now comes the Fātiḥa, the most important surah. Say it slowly, word by word. With every verse Allah answers you – you are speaking directly with Him.',
    sura: 'After the Fātiḥa you say a short surah you already know, for example Al-Ikhlāṣ: “Allah is One.” If you don’t know one yet, that’s fine – under “Learn surahs” you can practise step by step.',
    qunut: 'Now comes a special supplication, the qunūt. You ask Allah to guide you on the right path, to protect you and to help you.',
    ruku: 'Say “Allāhu akbar” and bow forward. Your back is straight like a table, your hands rest on your knees, and you look at the floor. Say three times: “Subḥāna rabbiya l-ʿaẓīm” – Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent.',
    itidal: 'Stand up straight again and say: “Samiʿa llāhu li-man ḥamidah” – Allah hears the one who praises Him. When you are standing: “Rabbanā wa laka l-ḥamd” – our Lord, all thanks are Yours.',
    sujud: 'Say “Allāhu akbar” and go down slowly: first your knees, then your hands, then your forehead and nose. Now you are very close to Allah. Say three times: “Subḥāna rabbiya l-aʿlā” – Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. Here you may also tell Him everything that makes you happy or sad.',
    jalsa: 'Sit up for a moment with your hands on your thighs. Breathe calmly and say: “Rabbi ghfir lī” – my Lord, forgive me. Then you go down once more.',
    tashahhud: 'Stay seated. Now you say the tashahhud: you greet Allah, the Prophet ﷺ and all good people. When you say “There is no god but Allah”, you raise your right index finger.',
    rise: 'Stand up again and say “Allāhu akbar”. A new rakʿah begins – like a new round of the prayer, again with the Fātiḥa, bowing and prostration.',
    salawat: 'Stay seated and say the ṣalawāt: you ask Allah to bless the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and his family – just as He blessed Ibrāhīm and his family.',
    dua: 'Now you may ask Allah for good things – for yourself, your parents, your friends and all people. For example: “Our Lord, give us good in this world and in the Hereafter.”',
    salam: 'Turn your head to the right and say “As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu llāh” – peace be upon you. Then to the left the same way. Every prayer ends like this: with a greeting of peace to everyone.',
    shahada: 'Well done! You are now clean and ready to pray. At the end you say the declaration of faith: There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His Messenger.',
    wudu: 'With water you make yourself clean – on the outside, and your heart becomes calm too.',
    wuduParts: {
      heart: 'Before you begin, say in your heart: “I am now washing for the prayer.” Then quietly say “Bismillāh” – in the name of Allah. And remember to save water: only let the tap run while you need it.',
      hands: 'First wash your hands up to the wrists – three times. Rub between your fingers too, just like washing your hands before eating. Always start with the right hand.',
      mouth: 'Take some water into your mouth with your right hand, rinse it well – your cheeks may move – and spit the water into the basin. You do this three times.',
      nose: 'With your right hand, gently draw a little water into your nose – not too hard! – and blow it out with your left hand. This three times as well.',
      face: 'Now your whole face: from the forehead, where your hair begins, to under your chin, and from one ear to the other. Three times – and no spot may stay dry, that is required.',
      armR: 'Wash your right arm from your fingertips to just above the elbow. The elbow is included! Three times, then the left arm.',
      armL: 'Now the left arm the same way: from your fingertips to just above the elbow, three times.',
      head: 'Wet your hands and wipe them over your head: from the forehead back to the neck and forward again. Here you don’t wash, you just wipe once.',
      ears: 'With your wet index fingers go through the inside of your ears, and with your thumbs over the backs of your ears. Once is enough.',
      footR: 'Now the right foot – best while sitting on the stool. Wash it up to just above the ankle, three times. Don’t forget between your toes: your little finger does that well.',
      footL: 'Finally the left foot the same way, up to just above the ankle and between the toes, three times.',
    },
  },
